# 中频词汇 List09
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023恋练有词
# 描述: 中频词汇List09核心词汇

{{episode}}{/ˈepɪsəʊd/}{插曲；一集}{The final episode of the series broke viewership records.}}
{{equivalent}}{/ɪˈkwɪvələnt/}{等价的；相当的}{One mile is roughly equivalent to 1.6 kilometers.}}
{{era}}{/ˈɪərə/}{时代；纪元}{We are living in the era of artificial intelligence.}}
{{error}}{/ˈerər/}{错误；过失}{The report contained several factual errors.}}
{{escape}}{/ɪˈskeɪp/}{逃跑；逃避}{The prisoners attempted to escape from the jail.}}
{{essence}}{/ˈesns/}{本质；精华}{In essence, the proposal is about reducing costs.}}
{{essential}}{/ɪˈsenʃl/}{必要的；本质的}{Sleep is essential for good health.}}
{{ethic}}{/ˈeθɪk/}{道德规范；伦理}{Business ethics are important for building trust.}}
{{ethnic}}{/ˈeθnɪk/}{民族的；种族的}{The city has a rich ethnic diversity.}}
{{eventually}}{/ɪˈventʃuəli/}{最终；终于}{After years of hard work, she eventually achieved her dream.}}
{{evident}}{/ˈevɪdənt/}{明显的；显然的}{It was evident that the plan was not working.}}
{{evil}}{/ˈiːvl/}{邪恶的；罪恶}{The novel explores the nature of good and evil.}}
{{exaggerate}}{/ɪɡˈzædʒəreɪt/}{夸张；夸大}{The media tends to exaggerate the severity of crises.}}
{{examine}}{/ɪɡˈzæmɪn/}{检查；审查}{The doctor examined the patient thoroughly.}}
{{excessive}}{/ɪkˈsesɪv/}{过度的；过多的}{Excessive drinking is harmful to your health.}}
{{exchange}}{/ɪksˈtʃeɪndʒ/}{交换；交易所}{They exchanged gifts during the holiday celebration.}}
{{exclusive}}{/ɪkˈskluːsɪv/}{排他的；独家的}{The magazine published an exclusive interview with the president.}}
{{exert}}{/ɪɡˈzɜːt/}{施加；发挥}{Parents exert a strong influence on their children's behavior.}}
{{exhaust}}{/ɪɡˈzɔːst/}{耗尽；排气}{The long hike exhausted everyone in the group.}}
{{exotic}}{/ɪɡˈzɒtɪk/}{异国的；奇异的}{The island is known for its exotic plants and animals.}}
{{expansion}}{/ɪkˈspænʃn/}{扩张；扩展}{The rapid expansion of the city led to traffic problems.}}
{{expense}}{/ɪkˈspens/}{费用；开支}{Travel expenses are covered by the company.}}
{{experiment}}{/ɪkˈsperɪmənt/}{实验；试验}{The experiment yielded unexpected but fascinating results.}}
{{expertise}}{/ˌekspɜːˈtiːz/}{专业知识；专长}{Her expertise in data analysis was invaluable.}}
{{explicit}}{/ɪkˈsplɪsɪt/}{明确的；清楚的}{The contract contains explicit terms and conditions.}}
{{exploitation}}{/ˌeksplɔɪˈteɪʃn/}{开发；剥削}{The exploitation of natural resources must be regulated.}}
{{explosion}}{/ɪkˈspləʊʒn/}{爆炸；激增}{There has been an explosion of interest in online learning.}}
{{exposure}}{/ɪkˈspəʊʒər/}{暴露；曝光}{Exposure to sunlight helps the body produce vitamin D.}}
{{extension}}{/ɪkˈstenʃn/}{延伸；延期}{The deadline has been given a one-week extension.}}
{{extent}}{/ɪkˈstent/}{程度；范围}{The extent of the damage is still being assessed.}}
